Jewish American Security Act aims to strengthen federal efforts to counter antisemitism and protect the Jewish community through measures involving education, security grants, threat assessments, and online platform transparency.","summary_threshold":50,"title":"Jewish American Security Act","viability":29.0,"viability_status":"active"},"date":"2026-05-19","detail":"Related bill","id":"119-s-4576","label":"S. 4576","title":"Jewish American Security Act","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/4576"}]},"selection":{"reason":"Impact scored and summarised by Gemini.","status":"analyzed"},"sources":{"latest":{"date":"2026-06-09","label":"Introduced in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr9211/BILLS-119hr9211ih.htm"},"other":[{"label":"This bill on Congress.gov","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/9211"}],"past":[]},"sponsor":{"chamber":"House","district":"10","id":"G000599","name":"Rep. Goldman, Daniel S.","party":"D","state":"NY"},"stage":"in_committee","stage_label":"Referred to committee","summary":"H.R. 9211, titled the \"Jewish American Security Act,\" seeks to strengthen federal efforts to counter antisemitism and protect the Jewish community through education, law enforcement coordination, and increased reporting and grant funding.","summary_detail":{"affected_groups":[{"effect":"Receive increased federal protection, enhanced security grant funding for community institutions and houses of worship, and targeted efforts to counter antisemitism online and offline.","group":"Jewish Americans and the Jewish Community"},{"effect":"Educational institutions receiving federal financial assistance must meet new Title VI compliance requirements, appoint coordinators, and adopt formal grievance procedures, while students gain access to awareness campaigns and expanded reporting channels.","group":"Students and Educational Institutions"},{"effect":"Platforms with at least 50 million unique monthly U.S. users must submit and publish detailed transparency reports on their content moderation practices regarding antisemitic content, enforced by the Federal Trade Commission.","group":"Large Online Platforms"},{"effect":"Eligible for federal grants to support increased policing, patrols, and training around houses of worship and at-risk religious institutions.","group":"State and Local Law Enforcement Agencies"}],"key_provisions":["Requires the Department of Education to designate an antisemitism coordinator, provide training and written reminders regarding Title VI obligations, conduct an awareness campaign, and establish a clearinghouse for campus safety and best practices.","Requires educational institutions receiving federal financial assistance to designate a Title VI coordinator, implement nondiscrimination and grievance procedures, and maintain records related to discrimination reports.","Increases authorizations and funding for the Department of Homeland Security's Nonprofit Security Grant Program to $1,000,000,000 for each of fiscal years 2027 through 2031, while easing certain percentage caps on security personnel.","Authorizes the Attorney General to award grants to state and local law enforcement agencies to support increased policing presence, patrols, and training for at-risk religious institutions.","Directs federal agencies (FBI, DHS, and the National Counterterrorism Center) to produce joint annual threat assessments on domestic and transnational antisemitic violent extremism.","Requires large online platforms with at least 50 million unique monthly users in the United States to publish regular transparency reports detailing their content moderation practices regarding antisemitic content."],"missing_information":["Specific details on the exact methods or algorithms the FTC will use to evaluate online platform compliance beyond general enforcement authorities.","Exact allocation formulas for how the increased Nonprofit Security Grant Program funds will be distri